.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH watch 1  "watch " 
.SH NAME
watch \- Watch a folder and import filesystem changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwatch\fR [\fB\-\-debounce\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-\-once\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-filters\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-paths\fR] [\fB\-\-filters\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Watch a folder and import filesystem changes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-debounce\-ms\fR \fI<DEBOUNCE_MS>\fR [default: 500]
Debounce changes in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<GLOB>\fR
Ignore a path glob; may be repeated
.TP
\fB\-\-once\fR
Process one event and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-filters\fR
Print the active filter configuration and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Evaluate paths against the filter rules without importing
.TP
\fB\-\-paths\fR \fI<PATHS>...\fR
Paths evaluated by \-\-dry\-run
.TP
\fB\-\-filters\fR \fI<FILTERS>\fR
Filter configuration (defaults to DATA_DIR/filters.toml)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

